            },
            "displayName": "Grant Ingersoll",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2008-01-16T16:47:41.734+0000",
          "updated": "2008-01-16T16:47:41.734+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12386397/comment/12559588",
          "id": "12559588",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Gack!  I recommended a bitset on Token previously, but I meant an elemental one... an int (32 bits) or a long (64 bits).\nHalf of the bits could be reserved for use by Lucene tokenizers, and half could be reserved for users.  I think an actual BitSet is too heavy-weight.\n\nJust provide a int or long Token.getFlags() and int or long Token.setFlags(), and nothing more (we don't need to do bit twiddling for users IMO)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=yseeley%40gmail.com",
            "name": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "key": "yseeley@gmail.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Yonik Seeley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2008-01-16T17:02:54.597+0000",
          "updated": "2008-01-16T17:02:54.597+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12386397/comment/12559589",
          "id": "12559589",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "I see two problems with this patch:\n\n1. Although in the patch you say that the \"type bits\" field added by the patch is completely separate from the String type information, you don't name them with sufficiently different names to distinguish them.\n\n2. The information encoded by BitSet is a set of <int,boolean> tuples.  These are opaque values.  In order for this to work, every tokenizer in the chain has to be aware of every other one's use of these.  This makes sharing hard.\n\nAt a minimum, there should be some way to declare who's using what bit for what purpose - maybe through a static hash table or something?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
